    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-ai-enabled-implantable-and-wearable-systems-for-closed-loop-precision-health-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - AI-Enabled Implantable and Wearable Systems for Closed-Loop Precision Health",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor - AI-Enabled Implantable and Wearable Systems for Closed-Loop Precision Health - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant or Associate Professor - AI-Enabled Implantable and Wearable Systems for Closed-Loop Precision Health - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor - AI-Enabled Implantable and Wearable Systems for Closed-Loop Precision Health 497060 Full-Time Electrical Engineering Department : Electrical and Computer Engineering Salary : Commensurate with Experience Description : The Department of Electrical and Computer Engineering (ECE) at the University of Houston (UH) invites applications for a tenure-track/tenure-eligible faculty position in AI-Enabled Implantable and Wearable Systems for Closed-Loop Precision Health at the Assistant or Associate Professor rank. The successful candidate will be appointed at the Assistant Professor (tenure-track) or Associate Professor (tenure-eligible) rank, based on experience and qualifications. The tenure home will be in ECE, with opportunities for collaborative appointments and research partnerships with the Department of Health and Human Performance in the College of Liberal Arts and Social Sciences, the Department of Pharmacological and Pharmaceutical Sciences in the College of Pharmacy, and the Tilman J. Fertitta Family College of Medicine. This position seeks an emerging research leader working at the intersection of implantable and wearable medical devices, bioelectronics, biomedical sensing, artificial intelligence, digital health, and precision therapeutics. Of particular interest are candidates developing systems that enable continuous acquisition of physiological, biochemical, biomechanical, or optical data and integrate these measurements with AI-guided analysis, therapeutic intervention, and assessment of biological response. A central research opportunity is the development of closed-loop precision health systems that integrate data acquisition, AI analysis, treatment decision, biological response assessment, and treatment optimization. The successful candidate is expected to develop innovative implantable and wearable bioelectronic platforms and collaborate with investigators in human health, pharmacology, and medicine to connect continuous sensing data with therapeutic interventions, molecular biomarkers, pharmacological response, and treatment-induced gene-expression changes. The successful candidate will be expected to establish an internationally recognized, externally funded research program; develop interdisciplinary collaborations across UH; pursue large multi-investigator and center-scale research opportunities; teach undergraduate and graduate courses; mentor graduate and undergraduate students; and contribute to the educational and research missions of the department and university. The research area has a broad and diversified funding ecosystem, including opportunities through NIH, NSF, ARPA-H, DoD, CPRIT, DPRIT, medical device companies, healthcare systems, translational research programs, and private foundations. Relevant research areas may include, but are not limited to: • Implantable and wearable medical devices • Soft, flexible, and biointegrated electronics • Biomedical sensors and instrumentation • AI and machine learning for healthcare • Agentic AI for adaptive health systems • Closed-loop therapeutic and neuromodulation systems • Physiological and biochemical monitoring • Multimodal biomedical data analytics • Digital biomarkers and precision medicine • Federated and privacy-preserving machine learning • Wireless and low-power biomedical systems • Translational medical device technologies The University of Houston is a Carnegie-designated Tier One public research university located in one of the nation's largest metropolitan areas. ECE maintains a strong and growing research portfolio, extensive interdisciplinary collaborations, and a strong record of graduate education, research translation, and industry engagement. UH is located in Houston, the fourth largest city in the United States, with access to a major industrial base, the Texas Medical Center, NASA, and a broad technology and innovation ecosystem. Houston offers exceptional opportunities for interdisciplinary research, industry collaboration, commercialization, and workforce development. The department seeks outstanding candidates with the potential for exceptional research, excellence in teaching, and effective mentoring of graduate and undergraduate students. Anticipated Start Date: Fall 2027, or as negotiated Qualifications Applicants must possess an earned doctorate in electrical engineering, biomedical engineering, computer engineering, computer science, or another closely related field at the time of appointment. Candidates should demonstrate strong potential for developing an externally funded, internationally recognized research program and for effective collaboration across disciplinary boundaries. For appointment at the Associate Professor level, candidates should have a demonstrated record of research excellence, external funding, scholarly impact, teaching, and professional leadership commensurate with appointment at that rank. Preference may be given to candidates who have demonstrated success in securing competitive research support, including NIH K99/R00, NSF CAREER, DoD Young Investigator, or comparable early-career or independent research funding. Required Attachments by Candidate: 1. Cover Letter / Letter of Application 2. Curriculum Vitae 3. Research Statement 4. Teaching Philosophy or Statement 5. Statement describing the candidate's vision for interdisciplinary collaboration 6. Names and contact information for professional references Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Should listed references be contacted, they will be asked to submit letters of recommendation. Employees are expected to have a home address in the state of Texas for the duration of their appointments. Official transcripts are required for a faculty appointment and will be requested upon selection of the final candidates. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. Individuals conducting research in critical infrastructure areas (i.e., communication infrastructure systems, cybersecurity systems, electric grid, hazardous waste treatment systems, and/or water treatment facilities) are subject to regular review to ensure the security and integrity of the research is maintained. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) d6b505b1 Last Name (required) 1f088f54 Email (required) c97b562e Cell number 92da3a50 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) Côte d’Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Curaçao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (+253) Dom