    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/assistant-or-associate-professor-pharmaceutics-or-medicinal-chemistry-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Pharmaceutics or Medicinal Chemistry",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Pharmaceutics or Medicinal Chemistry - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant or Associate Professor - Pharmaceutics or Medicinal Chemistry - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor - Pharmaceutics or Medicinal Chemistry 497074 Full-Time Pharmacological & Pharmaceutic Department : Pharmacological & Pharmaceutical Sciences Salary : Commensurate with experience Description : The Department of Pharmacological and Pharmaceutical Sciences (PPS) at the University of Houston invites applications for a full-time, tenure-track faculty position at the Assistant or Associate Professor level through the Presidential Frontier Faculty program ( https://www.uh.edu/provost/faculty/prospective-faculty/presidential-frontier-faculty/ ) in either Pharmaceutics or Medicinal Chemistry. The Presidential Frontier Faculty initiative is a university-wide interdisciplinary hiring campaign aimed at enhancing the UH research enterprise by integrating the strengths of existing faculty and infrastructure with strong early career new faculty hires. We strongly encourage applications from outstanding candidates with innovative, cross-disciplinary research programs. For Pharmaceutics, target areas broadly encompass pharmacokinetics, drug metabolism, formulation, and drug delivery for small molecules, biologics, and nucleic acid therapeutics. Applicants whose primary research focus is pharmacology or other biomedical fields—without a substantive core program in pharmaceutics or drug delivery—will not be considered a strong fit for this role. For Medicinal Chemistry, target areas broadly include chemical biology, biophysical medicinal chemistry, and synthetic medicinal chemistry. Driven by the momentum of the Cancer Prevention and Research Institute of Texas (CPRIT) and the upcoming Dementia Prevention and Research Institute of Texas (DPRIT), this opening presents an exceptional opportunity for researchers with strong expertise in cancer or neuroscience. PPS is housed in Health Building 2, a 300,000-square-foot, state-of-the-art facility on the main University of Houston campus. Faculty research programs benefit from exceptional laboratory space and cutting-edge core facilities, including a 600 MHz JEOL NMR and high-end mass spectrometers. Additional shared instrumentation includes a VisualSonics Vevo 3100 Preclinical Imaging System, PerkinElmer IVIS Lumina III XRMS Whole Animal Imaging System, state-of-the-art Orbitrap Exploris 480 High-Resolution Mass Spectrometers, AB Sciex 7500+ LC-MS/MS systems, confocal microscopes, Digital & QuantStudio RT-PCR systems, Agilent Seahorse XF metabolic analyzers, PhenoMasterNG metabolic/behavioral/physiological cages, Sartorius Octet R8, BioTek Cytation 10, Shimadzu HPLC, and an Opentrons Flex station. Departmental research strengths span pharmaceutics, medicinal chemistry, and pharmacology, covering pharmacokinetics, drug metabolism, PK/PD modeling, drug delivery, formulations, lead optimization, chemical biology, and molecular/cellular/in vivo pharmacology, providing ample opportunity for collaboration. Primary therapeutic areas of interest include cancer, neuroscience, immunology, cardiovascular, renal, skeletal muscle, infectious diseases, bone, and substance use disorders, though qualified candidates working in other therapeutic areas are also encouraged to apply. We seek candidates who demonstrate high potential for groundbreaking research, a strong commitment to graduate and professional education, and an eagerness to collaborate within the University of Houston's strategic research priority in Health. A proven record of scholarly productivity, prior research funding, and a well-defined strategy for securing extramural support will be considered favorably, with preference given to applicants who show a strong track record or exceptional potential for attracting extramural funding. Interested candidates should submit: (1) a cover letter briefly describing how their research aligns with the Department—particularly within the pharmaceutics and medicinal chemistry disciplines—and noting any specialized facility requirements, (2) a statement of research accomplishments and future research plans, (3) a standalone document detailing current, past, and pending research funding, (4) a statement outlining teaching experience, philosophy, and interests, (5) a current curriculum vitae, and (6) contact information for three professional references. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled. Notably, selected eligible recruits who show outstanding promise in cancer research may apply for Cancer Prevention & Research Institute (CPRIT) Recruitment of First-Time, Tenure-Track Faculty Members, which offer up to $2 million in funding. The University of Houston is a Carnegie-Designated Tier 1 public research university and a member institution of the world-renowned Texas Medical Center (TMC), which houses major academic research programs in cancer, genetics, and neuroscience with a significant focus on translational research. The TMC also provides excellent opportunities for collaborative biomedical research. With over 46,000 students, UH offers a comprehensive range of programs across 15 colleges, fostering innovation in fields such as energy, health, hospitality, business, education, law, STEM, and the humanities. Boasting top-tier faculty, state-of-the-art facilities, student success initiatives, and a strong commitment to community engagement, UH prepares students to thrive in a globally interconnected world while contributing impactful research and innovation to the region and beyond. The University's prime location in America's fourth-largest city supports extensive industry partnerships and experiential learning opportunities. Renowned for its Texas Medical Center, energy industry and NASA's Space Center, Houston is home to a vibrant cultural scene with world-class museums, theaters, and restaurants. Houston thrives as a hub for innovation, education, and arts, fostering a unique blend of community charm and modern progress. Qualifications: Eligible candidates must have earned a doctoral degree or equivalent degree in related discipline with relevant postdoctoral experience, an excellent publication record, scholarly productivity, and high potential to develop an extramurally funded research program. Rank and salary commensurate with experience. Duties & Responsibilities • Develop and maintain a strong, extramurally funded, independent research program. • Teach the Pharm D. professional program and graduate programs at the College of Pharmacy. • Engage in services at Department, College, and University committees. Provide external services in community, and professional organizations. • Supervise graduate students and post-doctoral fellows in research. Employees are expected to have a home address in the state of Texas for the duration of their appointments. Official transcripts are required for a faculty appointment and will be requested upon selection of the final candidates. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. Individuals conducting research in critical infrastructure areas (i.e., communication infrastructure systems, cybersecurity systems, electric grid, hazardous waste treatment systems, and/or water treatment facilities) are subject to regular review to ensure the security and integrity of the research is maintained. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply Apply now First Name (required) 072b9824 Last Name (required) e1665406 Email (required) 08a78db6 Cell number bc08d1b5 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1