      "title": "Instructional Assistant Professor - Organic Chemistry and General Chemistry",
      "description": "Instructional Assistant Professor - Organic Chemistry and General Chemistry - Houston, Texas, United States Instructional Assistant Professor - Organic Chemistry and General Chemistry - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Instructional Assistant Professor - Organic Chemistry and General Chemistry 496956 Full-Time Chemistry Department : Chemistry Salary : Commensurate with experience Description : The Department of Chemistry at the University of Houston invites applications for a non-tenure-track Instructional Assistant Professor position for Organic Chemistry and General Chemistry. The successful candidate will have a Ph.D. in organic chemistry, experience using Canvas course management software and Microsoft Teams, a strong commitment to chemistry education, and the ability to construct original, free-response midterm and final exams for organic chemistry lecture sections. Experience in teaching in-person university-level chemistry lecture courses is highly preferred but not required. The position emphasizes excellence in undergraduate teaching, development of instructional materials and assessments, and collaboration with faculty and university partners that support the teaching of chemistry. Job duties include the following: teach two large (>200 students) sections of Organic Chemistry I and/or II, or one section of Organic Chemistry and one section of general chemistry, in the fall and spring semesters; teach one section of Organic Chemistry I or II during Session 1 of the summer semester; construct original, free-response midterm and final exams for Organic Chemistry I and II lecture sections; and perform other teaching and service duties as assigned by the Chair of the Department. The successful candidate is also expected to participate in departmental, college, and university service activities appropriate to a non-tenure-track instructional faculty appointment and to engage in continuous improvement of the organic chemistry and general chemistry curricula, instructional practices, and student success initiatives. Application Documents: -A cover letter -A full curriculum vitae -A maximum two-page statement of teaching interests and experience -An optional additional document to demonstrate teaching effectiveness -Contact information for three professional references Employees are expected to have a home address in the state of Texas for the duration of their appointments. Official transcripts are required for a faculty appointment and will be requested upon selection of the final candidates. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. Individuals conducting research in critical infrastructure areas (i.e., communication infrastructure systems, cybersecurity systems, electric grid, hazardous waste treatment systems, and/or water treatment facilities) are subject to regular review to ensure the security and integrity of the research is maintained. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 2d06c605 Last Name (required) d147710f Email (required) dd0cb81a Cell number 4fcedc35 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Island