    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-behavioral-neuroscience-focus-on-memory-and-dementia-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Behavioral Neuroscience (focus on memory and dementia)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Behavioral Neuroscience (focus on memory and dementia) - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant Professor - Behavioral Neuroscience (focus on memory and dementia) - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant Professor - Behavioral Neuroscience (focus on memory and dementia) 496809 Full-Time Psychology Department : Psychology Salary : Commensurate with Experience Description : The Psychology Department at the University of Houston seeks applicants for a Presidential Frontier Faculty tenure-track Assistant Professor position, effective Fall 2027. The Presidential Frontier Faculty program is a university-wide interdisciplinary hiring campaign aimed at enhancing the UH research enterprise by integrating the strengths of existing faculty and infrastructure with strong early career new faculty hires. We seek a behavioral neuroscientist who uses animal models to investigate the mechanisms underlying memory function or impairment, particularly aging-related memory dysfunction, including neurodegenerative diseases such as Alzheimer’s and related dementias. The position will be a split appointment between Psychology and the Texas Institute for Measurement, Evaluation and Statistics (TIMES). TIMES is a university-level research center that supports faculty from multiple disciplines and departments, including Psychology. Applicants must hold a Ph.D. in psychology, neuroscience or a related field and have postdoctoral experience. Competitive candidates will have a strong publication record and an externally funded research program, which may include mentored fellowship awards or independent funding. The successful candidate is also expected to 1) collaborate with faculty within the department and across the university, particularly within the expanding neuroscience and biomedical research community; 2) contribute to the university’s strategic initiatives related to neurodegenerative disease and 3) demonstrate a strong commitment to teaching and mentoring. The Department of Psychology is a highly collegial group of nationally and internationally recognized tenure-track and research faculty committed to advancing science of the brain, mind and mental health. Our faculty conduct rigorous, externally funded research and our department consistently ranks in the top five in external funding at UH. We have over 3800 undergraduate majors and 130 PhD students across 4 areas: clinical; social, personality, and health (SPH); industrial organizational (IO); and developmental, cognitive and behavioral neuroscience (DCBN). The Department of Psychology provides state-of-the-art laboratory space within the Health 1 Building (H1) that includes wet lab space, animal housing, and an animal behavioral core as well as access to advanced core facilities across the UH campus, and abundant opportunities for collaboration within the university and with nearby institutions. The University of Houston is a large, urban public university with over 48,000 students. We are a Carnegie 1 research institution, with a strong and growing research enterprise driving innovation and discovery in a wide array of disciplines housed within 17 colleges. Our central location in America’s fourth-largest city facilitates industry partnerships, and collaborative opportunities in the Texas Medical Center, of which UH is a member. Houston is a vibrant city with world-class museums, performing arts and an exciting restaurant and live music scene. Review of applicants will begin on October 1, 2026 and will continue until the position is filled. Please direct queries about the position to J. Leigh Leasure, jlleasure@uh.edu To apply visit the link that follows: https://www.uh.edu/provost/faculty/prospective-faculty/index . Please include letter of interest, current curriculum vitae, research statement, representative papers, teaching statement, evidence of excellence in teaching. Employees are expected to have a home address in the state of Texas for the duration of their appointments. Official transcripts are required for a faculty appointment and will be requested upon selection of the final candidates. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. Individuals conducting research in critical infrastructure areas (i.e., communication infrastructure systems, cybersecurity systems, electric grid, hazardous waste treatment systems, and/or water treatment facilities) are subject to regular review to ensure the security and integrity of the research is maintained. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 88ac0b9f Last Name (required) 0ecce22e Email (required) a3e3aeed Cell number 94f0075f 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) Brunei (+673) Bulgaria (+359) Burkina Faso (+226) Burundi (+257) Cambodia (+855) Cameroon (+237) Canada (+1) Cape Verde (+238) Caribbean Netherlands (+599) Cayman Islands (+1) Central African Republic (+236) Chad (+235) Chile (+56) China (+86) Christmas Island (+61) Cocos (Keeling) Islands (+61) Colombia (+57) Comoros (+269) Congo - Brazzaville (+242) Congo - Kinshasa (+243) Cook Islands (+682) Costa Rica (+506) Côte d’Ivoire (+225) Croatia (+385) Cuba (+53) Curaçao (+599) Cyprus (+357) Czechia (+420) Denmark (+45) Djibouti (+253) Dominica (+1) Dominican Republic 