      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Law",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor - Law - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant or Associate Professor - Law - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant or Associate Professor - Law 496753 Full-Time Dean, Law Department : Dean, Law Salary : Commensurate with Experience Description : The University of Houston Law Center (UHLC) invites applications for a tenure-track Assistant/Associate Professor position to begin Fall 2027 term with 1L criminal law and 1L legislation and regulation and various upper level courses including especially family law, evidence, PR, and employment/labor law. Applicants for the position must hold a J.D. degree (or the equivalent) and should demonstrate the potential for success as a scholar, teacher, and future member of the community of the University of Houston Law Center (UHLC) and the University of Houston (UH) more broadly. Multiple hires at the tenure-track entry level are sought. These multiple positions require teaching coverage in 1L doctrinal courses, upper-level required courses, and bar topic courses. Candidates from across all doctrinal areas of law will be considered, but we have the greatest need in traditional first-year subjects, most critically in (1) criminal law, and (2) legislation and regulation (a 1L course called Statutory Interpretation and Regulation). The most critical needs in upper-level courses are these: family law; labor and employment; PR; and evidence. Other upper-level topics of special interest are these: administrative law; bankruptcy; copyright; disability & the law; employment discrimination; energy law; health law; international law; and wills & trusts. Willingness to teach anywhere in the core UHLC curriculum, including other 1L courses or other courses covered on the bar exam, is also a positive factor. Further information about the UHLC and its programs is available at: http://www.law.uh.edu. This search is coordinated by Professor Johnny Rex Buckles, the chair of UHLC’s faculty appointments committee. Interested applicants can send questions to Prof. Buckles at jbuckles@central.uh.edu. The UHLC boasts an accomplished and collegial faculty representing a wide range of backgrounds including 16 who are members of the American Law Institute. The UHLC’s 2026 entering class has the strongest credentials in the school’s history. Since Fall of 2022, the UHLC occupies a brand-new, world-class facility designed by award-winning architects. The UHLC is located in close proximity to the Texas Medical Center, the world’s largest medical complex and an international leader in health and life sciences. The City of Houston offers a lower overall cost of living, no state income tax, and an excellent job market with a wide-range of residents from all backgrounds as well as a world-class food scene. UH is a Carnegie-designated Tier One public research university. UH serves the globally competitive Houston and Gulf Coast Region by providing world-class faculty, experiential learning, and strategic industry partnerships. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) ba251151 Last Name (required) e843b4ca Email (required) 7b5d5d9d Cell number 57ffde3e 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) Barbados (+1) Belarus (+375) Belgium (+32) Belize (+501) Benin (+229) Bermuda (+1) Bhutan (+975) Bolivia (+591) Bosnia & Herzegovina (+387) Botswana (+267) Brazil (+55) British Indian Ocean Territory (+246) British Virgin Islands (+1) B