      "title": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Family Nurse Practitioner",
      "description": "Clinical Assistant Professor - Family Nurse Practitioner - Houston, Texas, United States Clinical Assistant Professor - Family Nurse Practitioner - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Clinical Assistant Professor - Family Nurse Practitioner 492429 Full-Time Deans Office - CON Department: Deans Office - CON Salary: Commensurate with experience Description: The University of Houston Andy and Barbara Gessner College of Nursing at Central Campus is seeking an outstanding candidate to teach in the new post masters, Doctor of Nursing Practice program. This 9-month, promotion eligible, non-tenure-track (PE-NTT) position is for a Family Nurse Practitioner with a DNP or PhD who has exceptional leadership, scholarship and excellence in teaching. The anticipated start date for the qualified applicant begins as early as August 2023 and the search will continue until the position is filled. Faculty responsibilities include: ongoing curriculum development and evaluation; classroom and clinical instruction in the undergraduate and graduate programs using on-site, simulation, on-line, and distance education strategies; some travel; participation in college and university committees; engaging in scholarship, service and academic advising. For more information go to the nursing website . The Gessner College of Nursing is proud of its excellent BSN, MSN, and DNP programs; innovative web-enhanced education; simulation laboratories; and supportive student environment for both face-to-face and distance learning. While the primary teaching site is the University of Houston, the Gessner College of Nursing has programming at the University of Houston at Sugar Land and the University of Houston at Katy locations. The ability to teach a variety of graduate and undergraduate specialty areas is a plus. Faculty work collaboratively and support each other in a pleasant environment. The University of Houston is a Carnegie Tier 1 public research university located close to major energy companies and the Texas Medical Center. Houston is the fourth largest city in the United States and has a first-rate recreational opportunities, excellent schools, and affordable housing. Qualifications 1. Doctorate in nursing or related field required. 2. Master's degree in nursing from a professionally accredited school of nursing if the doctorate is not in nursing. 3. National certification in clinical specialty area required. 4. Candidate must possess an unencumbered license as a registered nurse in Texas. 5. Minimum 2 years of clinical experience as a Family Nurse Practitioner required. 6. Excellent clinical and communication skills. 7. Minimum of 2 years teaching experience required. 8. Published in peer-reviewed articles. Required Attachments by Candidate Unofficial Transcripts, Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter/Letter of Application Notes to Applicant A minimum of three letters of recommendation are required. Provide contact information for three professional references who will be contacted by the search committee during the selection process. Work location : University of Houston at Central Campus Health 2 Building. Official transcripts are required for a faculty appointment and will be requested upon selection of the final candidate. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check drug screen and clinical readiness. The University of Houston System and its universities are an Equal Opportunity Institution. FAC002935 Apply now First Name (required) e483c8ae Last Name (required) 2aed68cd Email (required) 23c980aa Cell number 0e65681f 244 results found No results found Afghanistan (+93) Åland Islands (+358) Albania (+355) Algeria (+213) American Samoa (+1) Andorra (+376) Angola (+244) Anguilla (+1) Antigua & Barbuda (+1) Argentina (+54) Armenia (+374) Aruba (+297) Ascension Island (+247) Australia (+61) Austria (+43) Azerbaijan (+994) Bahamas (+1) Bahrain (+973) Bangladesh (+880) 